I., king of Syria, who ultimately came to the throne, according to the word of the Lord to Elijah (1 Kings 19:15), after he had put the king to death (2 Kings 8:15).","verses":21,"father":"","mother":"","v":[17,18]},{"id":"judah_1751","name":"Judah","also":"","summary":"Praise, the fourth son of Jacob by Leah.","verses":245,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[18,19]},{"id":"jehoshaphat_808","name":"Jehoshaphat","also":"Josaphat","summary":"The son and successor of Asa, king of Judah. After fortifying his kingdom against Israel (2 Chr. 17:1, 2), he set himself to cleanse the land of idolatry (1 Kings 22:43).","verses":69,"father":"Asa","mother":"Azubah","v":[18]},{"id":"ahaziah_121","name":"Ahaziah","also":"Jehoahaz, Azariah","summary":"The son of Joram, or Jehoram, and sixth king of Judah. Called Jehoahaz (2 Chr. 21:17; 25:23), and Azariah (2 Chr. 22:6). Guided by his idolatrous mother Athaliah, his reign was disastrous (2 Kings 8:24-29; 9:29).","verses":26,"father":"Jehoram","mother":"Athaliah","v":[18]},{"id":"jehoram_803","name":"Jehoram","also":"Joram","summary":"The eldest son and successor of Jehoshaphat, king of Judah. He reigned eight years (B.C. 892-885) alone as king of Judah, having been previously for some years associated with his father (2 Chr. 21:5, 20; 2 Kings 8:16).","verses":16,"father":"Jehoshaphat","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"amaziah_214","name":"Amaziah","also":"","summary":"The son and successor of Joash, and eighth king of the separate kingdom of Judah (2 Kings 14:1-4). He began his reign by punishing the murderers of his father (5-7; 2 Chr. 25:3-5).","verses":34,"father":"Joash","mother":"Jehoaddan","v":[21]},{"id":"jehozabad_812","name":"Jehozabad","also":"","summary":"The son of Shomer, one of the two conspirators who put king Jehoash to death in Millo in Jerusalem (2 Kings 12:21).","verses":2,"father":"Shimrith","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"shimeath_2683","name":"Shimeath","also":"","summary":"","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"shimrith_2724","name":"Shimrith","also":"Shomer","summary":"The mother of Jehozabad, who murdered Joash (2 Kings 12:21); called also Shimrith, a Moabitess (2 Chr. 24:26).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"zabad_1746","name":"Zabad","also":"Jozachar","summary":"The son of Shemath. He conspired against Joash, king of Judah, and slew him (2 Chr. 24:25, 26).","verses":2,"father":"Shimeath","mother":"","v":[21]}],"places":[{"id":"beersheba_170","name":"Beersheba","kind":"City","lat":31.245,"lon":34.84068,"summary":"Well of the oath, or well of seven, a well dug by Abraham, and so named because he and Abimelech here entered into a compact (Gen. 21:31). On re-opening it, Isaac gave it the same name (Gen. 26:31-33).","verses":32,"v":[1]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[1,17,18]},{"id":"gath_442","name":"Gath","kind":"City","lat":31.69353,"lon":34.84388,"summary":"A wine-vat, one of the five royal cities of the Philistines (Josh. 13:3) on which the ark brought calamity (1 Sam. 5:8, 9; 6:17). It was famous also as being the birthplace or residence of Goliath (1 Sam. 17:4).","verses":32,"v":[17]},{"id":"syria_1122","name":"Syria","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":37.5,"lon":37.5,"summary":"(Heb. Aram), the name in the Old Testament given to the whole country which lay to the north-east of Phoenicia, extending to beyond the Euphrates and the Tigris.","verses":64,"v":[17,18]},{"id":"silla_1095","name":"Silla","kind":"River","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.2349